WildBuzzard corresponding source is published at:

https://github.com/openresearchtools/wildbuzzard

For a browser-only artifact build, use the exact WildBuzzard commit recorded in
browser-artifact-manifest.txt. A full release-set release-manifest.json also
records the exact commits for the separately distributed search extensions and
command-line packages. Complete source and build inputs for bundled third-party
code are carried in the repository or in the source and provenance artifacts
published beside the browser package.

The browser executable implements its shell command transport in
browser/app/WildBuzzardCommandLine.cpp, using the in-tree JsonCpp library.
Browser commands and workflows execute in Gecko. Their complete source and
the JsonCpp license are included in the browser source tree.

The independently installed buzzard-search and buzzard-minijtt releases publish
their own license, provenance, and corresponding-source artifacts. Their
sources are not browser payload. The browser package carries the native
qBittorrent/libtorrent runtime as a distinct GPL-2.0-only program together with
its component licenses and source-offer metadata; its corresponding-source
archives are published beside the browser package.

Tor's exact pinned source is distributed as
wildbuzzard-tor-0.4.9.11-source.tar. The installed Tor provenance binds that
archive, the native binary, and notices/tor-notices/THIRD-PARTY.json, which
identifies its statically linked OpenSSL, libevent, and zlib dependencies and
includes their exact copyright and license texts. The source archive is an
external release artifact and is not installed in the browser package.
The exact Brave adblock-resources and uBlock Origin corresponding source used
to generate the bundled blocker assets is distributed as
wildbuzzard-blocker-assets-source.tar.xz in that release set.
